<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<topic id="f3e5c0d1-beec-42fe-859a-2331662441bf" revisionNumber="1">
  <developerConceptualDocument
    xmlns="http://ddue.schemas.microsoft.com/authoring/2003/5"
    xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">

				<definitionTable>
					<definition>
						The installer copies the DemiCode Scheduler component assemblies and
						documentation for use on a development workstation or a build server. The installer
						can optionally install the component assembly in the Global Assembly Cache
						(GAC).
					</definition>
					<definition>
						Once installed, you can start using DemiCode Scheduler in your project by adding
						a reference to the DemiCode.Scheduling assembly (DemiCode.Scheduling.dll). The
						file is by default installed in the <legacyBold>DemiCode\Scheduler 1.1</legacyBold> folder in
						your <legacyBold>Program Files</legacyBold> folder. (For a computer running an english copy of Windows,
						this would usually be <legacyBold>C:\Program Files\DemiCode\Scheduler 1.1</legacyBold>.)
					</definition>
					<definition>
						Use the classes in the DemiCode.Scheduling assembly to create the scheduling functionality
						you want, and compile your project. DemiCode Scheduler can be initialized either
						<link xlink:href="c2259bf9-d765-4b73-afda-cbae2bf81a86">automatically using a configuration (.config) file</link>
						or plain XML, or <link xlink:href="2d6be93e-3019-45b3-aee0-4e5589703421">programmatically using the class library</link> from any .NET 2.0 compliant language. See <link xlink:href="ac8cf6b9-a48f-4b86-b13d-2303a63255aa">samples</link>, <link xlink:href="d9a6a49a-098b-4d25-aa79-eb78b4634e34" />
						and <externalLink>
                    		<linkText>class library reference</linkText>
    						<linkUri>R_Project.htm</linkUri>
    						<linkTarget>_self</linkTarget>
						</externalLink> sections for more information
						on this.
					</definition>
					<definition>
						When deploying your application, you must make sure the DemiCode.Scheduling assembly
						is available from your assembly. The DemiCode.Scheduling assembly should automatically
						be copied to the project output directory when you compile your application. (If
						you have installed the DemiCode.Scheduling assembly in the GAC on your development
						workstation or build server, you may need to perform special steps.) See the <link xlink:href="0de6046f-c5e3-4dc8-abd8-1b9a8d7d68c7">deployment</link> section for more information.
					</definition>
				</definitionTable>
				
							
			<section>
		<title>Skip right to the code</title>
		<content>
				
			
				<link xlink:href="c2259bf9-d765-4b73-afda-cbae2bf81a86">Set up the scheduler using a configuration file.</link><para/>
				<link xlink:href="2d6be93e-3019-45b3-aee0-4e5589703421">Set up the scheduler programmatically using the class library.</link>
			
			</content>
				</section>
				

